				<element type="warning_sequence">16</element>
                <text type="warning_situation">
				<p>MODERATE FLOODING LIKELY AT ISISFORD FROM WEDNESDAY AFTERNOON</p>
<p>MINOR FLOODING CONTINUING AT RETREAT</p>

				<p/>
				<p>Rainfall over the last week across the upper reaches of the Barcoo River catchment has resulted in river level rises and areas of flooding.</p>
<p/>
<p>Along the Barcoo River, renewed river level rises are occurring at Coolagh. Minor flooding is continuing at Isisford, where moderate flooding is likely from Wednesday afternoon as upstream flows continue to arrive.</p>
<p/>
<p>Along the lower Barcoo River, minor flooding is occurring at Retreat. Further rises are possible over the coming week as upstream flows continue to arrive.</p>

				<p/>

                </text>
                <element type="severity">Moderate</element>
